      "writtenOn": "2022-10-07T17:08:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmmm I\u0027m not sure what we want to do here. So I imagine in Dawn we maybe have two use cases.\n\n1) The client wants to give us a wgpu::Texture and thus we can use that texture for many purposes depending on usage support (rendering, sampling, copying, etc.).\n\n2) The client only has a TextureView (I think this comes from if they are using Dawn to manage a swapchain for them). This has a lot more limited uses than a Texture does.\n\nSo in Ganesh we handled this by having two different classes: GrBackendTexture (case 1) and GrBackendRenderTarget (case 2). I wonder if we want two separate classes for Graphite as well or just keep it all in one class. If we kept it in one class I\u0027m not sure how much introspection (to know which case we\u0027re in) we\u0027d need before we get it fully wrapped in a Texture/TextureProxy. It\u0027s possible it is fairly limited/no needed so just having one class may be nice. If there are advantages to having two distinct classes internally in Skia we should try and figure that out. FWIW GL will have a similar issue needing to handle passing in FBOs.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 34,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 34,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "25523bb79055f8a5e5de372fb827d290723639e4",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
