        "id": 7953
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-07T19:03:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "dawn is integrated with glfw, `wgpu::glfw::SetupWindowAndGetSurfaceDescriptor()` can be used to create `wgpu::Surface` and `wgpu::SwapChain` on most platforms (but glfw doesnt support Android, maybe not support IOS as well). See the implementation of `wgpu::glfw::SetupWindowAndGetSurfaceDescriptor()`, seems we only need to create an extra `CAMetalLayer` for creating `wgpu::Surface` for Metal. For Windows, X11 and Wayland, `wgpu::Surface` can just be created from the native Window directly. Seems it is not too bad.\n\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/glfw/utils.cpp;l\u003d50;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d1",
